{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032152-roll20-for-cofd-tips-tricks","id":1032152,"title":"Roll20 for CofD - Tips & Tricks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-15T08:52:36-08:00","id":1032152,"title":"Roll20 for CofD - Tips & Tricks","content":"I needed to roll some dices by net with my players. Wanted to use <a href=\"http://rpgroller.com/nwod/\" target=\"_blank\">NWoD Dice Roller</a>, but it freezed for few minutes. In the meanwhile I setup the chronicles page on Roll20 - and hit the wall. It's... enormous - and I only need to roll some e-dices from time to time. So can someone show me how to make players to roll those few d10s? Best with those shiny 3D dices. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T09:59:45-08:00","id":1032184,"title":"","content":"You can get a wod character sheet with dice reroller built in theres two I think on there you you choose the nwod one that has a selection of splat templates.<br /> <br /> Alternatively you can use these codes: n= number of dice to roll.<br /> <br /> /r nd10&gt;8! Or /r {nd10!}&gt;8<br /> To show successes 8 and above and rerolls 10s<br /> <br /> 9agains<br /> /r {nd10!&gt;9}&gt;8 or /r nd10&gt;8!&gt;9<br /> <br /> For 8 agains you should beable to just replace the 9 with 8.<br /> <br /> Rote action:<br /> /r {nd10ro 8 <br /> You have to reroll your own 10s though.<br /> <br /> It also has macros you can use if you know how","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T10:06:41-08:00","id":1032191,"title":"","content":"Don't use 3d dices: results shows only after they rolled. But if you insist: there inset &quot;my setting&quot; with styled gear as icon. Here two check boxes : &quot;enable 3d dice&quot; and &quot;automatically roll 3d dice&quot;. Maybe (not checked) each player should enable this.<br /> In &quot;my collection&quot; inset you can create macros for quick roll (for NPC or other needs). Body of macros should be contain formula<br /> /r {10d10!}&gt;8<br /> where you change only number of dices<br /> and for chance-dice<br /> /r {1d10!}&gt;10f1<br /> For meaning that's only one player and GM can see roll you use key no &quot;/r&quot; but &quot;/gr&quot;<br /> In charsheet (journal inset) you can choose combinations of any two attributes or attributes and skill or attributes, skill and special pool just clicking on them. And there dice roller section - when you click on dice icon then windows with modifier popup and for roll you can just press &quot;submit&quot;. It's bit laging - way quicker to use macroses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MutedMirth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can get a wod character sheet with dice reroller built in theres two I think on there you you choose the nwod one that has a selection of splat templates.</div> </div> </div> </div>nWoD charsheet and CofD charsheet definitely use different attack mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-15-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T13:10:51-08:00","id":1032292,"title":"","content":"Yeah, figure out what kind of rolls do you want to automate and write up macros. I do that for our Legend of Five Rings games.<br /> EDIT<br /> You can create a macro that asks how many dice you want to roll; it's pretty simple.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T02:48:04-08:00","id":1032559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>OsuNeko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032152-roll20-for-cofd-tips-tricks?p=1032191#post1032191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> nWoD charsheet and CofD charsheet definitely use different attack mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but I remember one of them I think wasn't called chronicles and it has nwod and chronicles options with defence plus other choices. The only thing I couldn't get to work was adding the weapon modifyer after the roll and not added to the roll in the sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11719-mutedmirth","name":"MutedMirth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:14:30-08:00","id":1032581,"title":"","content":"If i recall correctly there different kind of charsheets (you should choose when create game). One of them roll damage modifier other add damage modifier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12029,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","user":"OsuNeko","date":". 01-16-2017, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T04:56:58-08:00","id":1032590,"title":"","content":"There's a character sheet for CofD built by the Roll20 staff - I'd recommend you use that one (only has specific fields for vanilla / Requiem / Forsaken, but the vanilla has enough room for my group to use it for Beast).<br /> <br /> Also, one thing that might get lost - Handouts are a perfectly fine way to track Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:57:57-08:00","id":1032856,"title":"","content":"Is it too brash, brazen, and soulless of me to ask if somebody could make a character sheet with editable skills for use with historical campaigns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9849,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","user":"Aristarkos","date":". 01-16-2017, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T13:42:55-08:00","id":1032889,"title":"","content":"Make Macros:<br /> <br /> Eight Again Macro:<br /> /em Eight Again: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!&gt;8]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Nine Again Macro:<br /> /em Nine Again: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!&gt;9]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Ten Again/Normal Roll Macro:<br /> /em Normal Roll: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Chance Die Macro:<br /> /em Chance Roll: [[1d10sd&gt;10]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> You can pin these making them buttons, and each will prompt for number of dice you want to roll and what the roll is for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T15:47:08-08:00","id":1032963,"title":"","content":"Also, each token can have up to 3 customizable &quot;resource bars&quot;. They are great for tracking resources like Mana, Blood and other things that are expressed in numbers and go up and down. Would be good for Wounds if they were, well, you know, numbers. <br /> if you want quick and dirty way to track wounds on multiple creatures, just edit their names to include / X * in appropiate amounts to track who is wounded how much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T18:08:52-08:00","id":1033775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032152-roll20-for-cofd-tips-tricks?p=1032889#post1032889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make Macros:<br /> <br /> Eight Again Macro:<br /> /em Eight Again: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!&gt;8]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Nine Again Macro:<br /> /em Nine Again: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!&gt;9]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Ten Again/Normal Roll Macro:<br /> /em Normal Roll: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Chance Die Macro:<br /> /em Chance Roll: [[1d10sd&gt;10]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> You can pin these making them buttons, and each will prompt for number of dice you want to roll and what the roll is for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are amazing!!!! Thank you so much! You posted this just as I was starting to try to figure this thing out for this weekend's game!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T16:42:40-08:00","id":1034318,"title":"","content":"So, I've been running nWoD games using the Roll20 board for quite some time now and I'm pretty proud of my board set-up. I figured I'd share it for some inspiration. This is my board for a Vampire the Requiem game I'm running.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://s30.postimg.org/8z061cg0h/Roll20_board.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I use the bars to track blood, willpower and beats for each player. I use the little icons on each character portrait to track health with a corresponding symbol for each damage type. (It's not a perfect system, but it was the best visual way to track it that I found.) The conditions the characters have are listed beneath with a corresponding handout that has the description of all the conditions for reference. I use the macros that were already shared for rolling, and I've written up a ton of lil rule cheat sheets as handouts for quick reference.<br /> <br /> And for Vampire here, I've added their touchstones underneath their pictures. I've been working on permutations of this basic set-up for the various lines.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, the new Roll20 Character Sheets simplified a lot of this, but this system has been working for me really well for the past year. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4497-tellme_tellme","name":"TellMe_TellMe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4497_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T17:06:28-08:00","id":1034332,"title":"","content":"That looks awesome, your players are lucky to have you has a GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12860-your3rdshadow","name":"Your3rdShadow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T02:02:58-08:00","id":1034487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1032152-roll20-for-cofd-tips-tricks?p=1032889#post1032889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make Macros:<br /> <br /> Eight Again Macro:<br /> /em Eight Again: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!&gt;8]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Nine Again Macro:<br /> /em Nine Again: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!&gt;9]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Ten Again/Normal Roll Macro:<br /> /em Normal Roll: [[?{pool size|0}d10sd&gt;8!]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> Chance Die Macro:<br /> /em Chance Roll: [[1d10sd&gt;10]] for ?{Action}<br /> <br /> You can pin these making them buttons, and each will prompt for number of dice you want to roll and what the roll is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for these. They've certainly added to my Roll20 games <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T09:47:51-08:00","id":1034669,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/cZbCLLy.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> So here is mine. I use cards for fuel, willpower and beats as you can see on the lower right side of the board. And handouts are a lifesaver when it comes to conditions. I also have few of the empty with permisions set for players to edit. That way I can tell them what this new condition is all about and then they write it up when I continue with the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-09T12:13:23-07:00","id":1102067,"title":"","content":"I know this thread is old but thanks for the macro tips. I've been using the old /r {Xd10!}&gt;8! macro for ages and thus my macro bar was loaded with 1-10 and then gm1-10. I always wanted to make a single macro with a dice quarry but ?{Number of Dice} never worked.. I had no idea it was ?{pool size}! So thanks to Rani for that one, you beautiful thing you!<br /> <br /> And while we're sharing.. here's my V:tR Roll20 front page, featuring my 3 players, Mitchell the Ordo Mekhet, Alexandria the Crone Gangrel, and Jade the Carthian Daeva. We've had tuns of fun with these characters the setting of Los Angeles. Other (not visible to player) pics are for common NPCs, like Mitchell's ghouls 'Speak' and 'See', their local Reagent and each of their Sires.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/SEmLQuM.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","user":"Xaielao","date":". 06-09-2017, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T14:54:52-07:00","id":1103291,"title":"","content":"Here is mine. I tried really hard to have at my disposal the most critical information regarding rules, NPCs and PCs. I've translated to Spanish all the Chronicles of Darkness Conditions, pasted them as individual Handouts, and collected them in a 'Rules\\Conditions' subfolder. My three player characters are <b>Ruby</b>, a Moros journalist; <b>Berith</b>, a Mastigos occult broker; and <b>KayGee</b>, a hacker from Network Zero who's way over his head in all this. We used to have a Promethean and a Beast, but both quitted soon after the chronicle started.<br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iXzCBkD.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T12:32:39-07:00","id":1103582,"title":"","content":"Oh I like that background. A fog-shrouded city at night. Very moody <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1824-xaielao","name":"Xaielao","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1824_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}